        <fields>
            <name>txtRenewBillingContracts</name>
            <fieldText>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;{!nRecords} Billing Contracts are selected for renewal, click &apos;Next&apos; to start the renewal process. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Only Billing Contracts with a yearly billing period are processed; Lines that have a recurring product will be inheritted from the current Billing Contract; l&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;ines that have a &apos;One-Off&apos; will be ignored while renewing. In case of multiple selected Billing Contracts, the renewal will process in the background. A single Billing Contract will process immediately. In a normal renewal-mode, without overriding the product and dates, it is possible to combine Billing Contracts of different types.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</fieldText>
            <fieldType>DisplayText</fieldType>
            <styleProperties>
                <verticalAlignment>
                    <stringValue>top</stringValue>
                </verticalAlignment>
                <width>
                    <stringValue>12</stringValue>
                </width>
            </styleProperties>
        </fields>
        <fields>
            <name>IsOverrideProduct</name>
            <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
            <defaultValue>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </defaultValue>
            <fieldText>Override Product</fieldText>
            <fieldType>InputField</fieldType>
            <inputsOnNextNavToAssocScrn>UseStoredValues</inputsOnNextNavToAssocScrn>
            <isDisabled>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </isDisabled>
            <isRequired>true</isRequired>
            <styleProperties>
                <verticalAlignment>
                    <stringValue>top</stringValue>
                </verticalAlignment>
                <width>
                    <stringValue>12</stringValue>
                </width>
            </styleProperties>
        </fields>
        <fields>
            <name>Fulfilment_Section1</name>
            <fieldType>RegionContainer</fieldType>
            <fields>
                <name>Fulfilment_Section1_Column1</name>
                <fieldType>Region</fieldType>
                <fields>
                    <name>txtOverrideProduct</name>
                    <fieldText>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;font-size: 18px; color: rgb(189, 23, 23);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Caution&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; color: rgb(189, 23, 23);&quot;&gt;You choose to override the product, optionally also the start date and invoice date. This may be applicable for example in case of a rate change. When you override these values, your entries will apply to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;font-size: 14px; color: rgb(189, 23, 23);&quot;&gt;all Billing Contracts ({!nRecords})&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; color: rgb(189, 23, 23);&quot;&gt; that are selected for renewal. Also, for this scenario, please make sure that all selected Billing Contracts are of the same type. Proceed only if this is the case.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</fieldText>
                    <fieldType>DisplayText</fieldType>
                    <styleProperties>
                        <verticalAlignment>
                            <stringValue>top</stringValue>
                        </verticalAlignment>
                        <width>
                            <stringValue>12</stringValue>
                        </width>
                    </styleProperties>
                </fields>
                <fields>
                    <name>uiLineTop</name>
